WEBVTT

1
00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:43.621
Helaena.

2
00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:46.958
Helaena.

3
00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:49.586
Helaena.

4
00:02:57.969 --> 00:02:59.637
I'm sorry to disturb your rest.

5
00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:02.681
Have you heard word from my mother?

6
00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:03.641
No.

7
00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:06.144
Nor do I expect to. until...

8
00:03:18.573 --> 00:03:21.701
Did Aemond ask you
to ride into battle with him?

9
00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:28.333
Lord Corlys imagined he would.

10
00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:34.047
When I was a girl. I wanted to fly.

11
00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:37.217
But now. when...

12
00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.094
when I'm with Dreamfyre...

13
00:03:44.432 --> 00:03:45.517
it's...

14
00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.020
and then too much.

15
00:03:53.608 --> 00:03:57.194
I think our father felt the same way.

16
00:03:57.195 --> 00:04:00.697
He renounced the strength of dragons
and embraced a quieter life.

17
00:04:00.698 --> 00:04:02.534
He did not wish to be changed.

18
00:04:03.785 --> 00:04:07.956
You believe the dragons
alter us in some way?

19
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:11.918
You now have many dragons.

20
00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:15.380
Are you yourself not altered?

21
00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:17.674
No.

22
00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:21.678
Well. I do not wish to be.

23
00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:27.015
I wished only to put an end to our contest

24
00:04:27.016 --> 00:04:29.269
and restore us to our proper order.

25
00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:33.356
Helaena.

26
00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:38.486
Sister. I believe that you...

27
00:04:39.696 --> 00:04:42.240
may be a dreamer.

28
00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.659
That you...

29
00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.287
see things.

30
00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:52.834
I see flashes sometimes.

31
00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.920
Some clearer than others.

32
00:04:57.755 --> 00:04:59.299
What did you see last?

33
00:05:02.218 --> 00:05:03.553
A gray mare.

34
00:05:06.514 --> 00:05:07.515
Mm-hmm.

35
00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:12.103
What of Daemon? Have you seen him?

36
00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.648
Hm?

37
00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:18.735
The Winter Wolves. then.

38
00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:21.446
Or Tumbleton.

39
00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.574
Will Ormund Hightower be brought to heel?

40
00:05:25.575 --> 00:05:27.159
I don't know.

41
00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:29.746
You don't know? Or you will not say?

42
00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:38.837
You may refuse me as your sister.

43
00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.547
but I may compel you as your queen.

44
00:05:40.548 --> 00:05:42.926
Now. tell me what you know!

45
00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:48.096
Tell me there has been no mistake.
that I will prevail.

46
00:05:48.097 --> 00:05:50.224
as the gods must surely intend.
Tell me.

47
00:06:33.643 --> 00:06:34.769
Mother.

48
00:06:36.145 --> 00:06:39.107
I told you I would come. if I could.

49
00:06:41.359 --> 00:06:44.278
Were you not taken captive?

50
00:06:46.531 --> 00:06:47.907
Your sister was taken.

51
00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.703
But I managed to stay hidden. to escape.

52
00:06:53.997 --> 00:06:56.791
You have been so clever
to remain here undiscovered.

53
00:06:58.251 --> 00:06:59.877
I thought all had forsaken me.

54
00:07:11.556 --> 00:07:13.182
How could I forsake...

55
00:07:13.975 --> 00:07:15.143
my best...

56
00:07:16.686 --> 00:07:18.146
and truest son?

57
00:07:20.648 --> 00:07:22.567
The city has fallen. Aemond.

58
00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.654
You're all I have left.

59
00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:43.504
The road has been long and perilous.
so I'll be glad of a bed.

60
00:07:45.882 --> 00:07:47.633
What of Aegon?

61
00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:52.430
Aegon is most likely dead.

62
00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.185
I did all I could.

63
00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.526
And for you.

64
00:08:12.575 --> 00:08:14.451
But I have failed you. Aemond.

65
00:08:14.452 --> 00:08:15.453
No.

66
00:08:17.288 --> 00:08:19.372
- I was too young.
- Never.

67
00:08:19.373 --> 00:08:20.958
I was just a child.

68
00:09:08.297 --> 00:09:11.884
And in this moment. I will give you a son.

69
00:09:14.345 --> 00:09:15.721
Aemond.

70
00:09:22.103 --> 00:09:23.479
Aemond.

71
00:09:24.689 --> 00:09:26.691
- What have you seen?
- Please.

72
00:09:49.881 --> 00:09:51.299
Aemond.

73
00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:24.916
Open the gates!

74
00:10:45.353 --> 00:10:47.229
They've crossed the Blackwater Rush.

75
00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:49.397
- How many?
- Twenty thousand.

76
00:10:49.398 --> 00:10:51.025
A day's march away. Two at most.

77
00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:57.657
So. your dim but ambitious Dornish friend
died in the mud for nothing.

78
00:10:58.699 --> 00:10:59.866
That is no matter.

79
00:10:59.867 --> 00:11:03.204
I have a piece on the board now
that will bring the bitch to her knees.

80
00:11:05.998 --> 00:11:07.541
And what is that?

81
00:11:44.787 --> 00:11:46.205
- My prince--
- Move!

82
00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:51.711
Where is she? Where's Rhaena?

83
00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.963
I see we are dispensing with courtesies.

84
00:11:54.964 --> 00:11:56.465
Is she here?

85
00:11:57.591 --> 00:12:01.678
She flew. just after I sent to you.

86
00:12:01.679 --> 00:12:03.305
I could not hold her.

87
00:12:03.306 --> 00:12:05.933
Put her in chains if you have to.
lock her in a cell.

88
00:12:07.226 --> 00:12:09.060
Do you imagine it's so easy
to force a dragonrider

89
00:12:09.061 --> 00:12:10.813
to do what she does not wish?

90
00:12:12.148 --> 00:12:13.440
She exposes me. too.

91
00:12:13.441 --> 00:12:15.442
She beseeched me with tears in her eyes.

92
00:12:15.443 --> 00:12:17.320
swore that she would
remain here in hiding.

93
00:12:19.071 --> 00:12:20.990
Talk of a dragonrider is rife in the Vale.

94
00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:24.701
The villagers gossip
of a wild girl in the mountains

95
00:12:24.702 --> 00:12:26.244
living amongst nettles and sheep.

96
00:12:26.245 --> 00:12:28.371
I am finished with the matter.

97
00:12:28.372 --> 00:12:30.165
It is in my best interest now
to alert the queen

98
00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:31.667
- to her flight.
- No.

99
00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:35.128
You may blunt Rhaenyra's wrath.
but you will not evade it.

100
00:12:35.129 --> 00:12:36.130
Give me a day.

101
00:12:43.804 --> 00:12:45.222
Please.

102
00:12:48.684 --> 00:12:51.896
She has been here and there
seeking news of Vhagar.

103
00:12:53.564 --> 00:12:55.607
There's word of a sighting
near Fairmarket.

104
00:12:55.608 --> 00:12:57.360
so I can only assume...

105
00:13:04.492 --> 00:13:06.452
We are two days behind Aemond at best.

106
00:13:07.453 --> 00:13:10.289
I have long tired
of this endless searching.

107
00:13:11.874 --> 00:13:15.001
I cannot help but think
I'm being punished by Rhaenyra.

108
00:13:15.002 --> 00:13:16.962
or at least sent far from her sight.

109
00:13:18.798 --> 00:13:21.133
She thinks of us
only as tools to be wielded.

110
00:13:22.927 --> 00:13:26.763
I wondered. my lady.
if I might beg you for a kindness.

111
00:13:26.764 --> 00:13:29.974
My father wishes for Alyn and me
to be legitimized

112
00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:31.644
and take the Velaryon name.

113
00:13:32.395 --> 00:13:34.605
The queen is being reluctant.

114
00:13:35.481 --> 00:13:37.316
You know my standing after the Gullet.

115
00:13:38.234 --> 00:13:40.444
I do not think my words
would have much sway with her.

116
00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:44.073
But your father. perhaps.

117
00:13:45.241 --> 00:13:48.035
Why this concern now
with names and titles?

118
00:13:49.203 --> 00:13:50.412
I understand your grievance.

119
00:13:50.413 --> 00:13:52.622
but surely. you have
a better thing in your dragon

120
00:13:52.623 --> 00:13:54.874
than any lordly appellation.

121
00:13:54.875 --> 00:13:57.127
It is only that if
either of us were to marry.

122
00:13:57.128 --> 00:13:58.254
That is...

123
00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:03.300
if either of us gained the favor
of some highborn lady.

124
00:14:05.928 --> 00:14:08.931
He has spoken to you. then. Your brother.

125
00:14:17.606 --> 00:14:19.233
Is it Vhagar?

126
00:14:22.862 --> 00:14:23.863
No.

127
00:14:24.447 --> 00:14:26.990
I did not think us like
to escape the Red Keep.

128
00:14:26.991 --> 00:14:29.618
But Ser Adrian remained
steadfast and resolute.

129
00:14:31.078 --> 00:14:33.413
He led us to a secret gate

130
00:14:33.414 --> 00:14:36.040
and I had enough coin with me for horses.

131
00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:37.876
We tried to remain off the roads.

132
00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:41.963
but the forests have become
impassable in places.

133
00:14:41.964 --> 00:14:43.549
There are wild men in the woods now.

134
00:14:44.467 --> 00:14:46.843
I would not have arrived here
if it wasn't for him.

135
00:14:46.844 --> 00:14:49.721
Rhaenyra took the castle.
but he remained loyal.

136
00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:51.806
He helped me at great risk
to his own person.

137
00:14:51.807 --> 00:14:52.933
He is a gr--

138
00:14:56.979 --> 00:14:58.355
Have I offended you?

139
00:15:03.194 --> 00:15:04.361
No.

140
00:15:10.951 --> 00:15:12.578
You are all I have left.

141
00:15:28.427 --> 00:15:30.345
This is he.

142
00:15:30.346 --> 00:15:32.514
my protector and guide. Ser Adrian.

143
00:15:32.515 --> 00:15:33.849
Your Grace.

144
00:15:37.895 --> 00:15:38.896
Mm.

145
00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.451
Well. it seems I owe you a debt.

146
00:15:55.246 --> 00:15:57.706
I did only as my conscience demanded.

147
00:15:59.875 --> 00:16:02.169
The queen dowager was treated shamefully.

148
00:16:13.514 --> 00:16:14.557
Aemond!

149
00:16:24.525 --> 00:16:26.193
Sorry. Mother.

150
00:16:28.237 --> 00:16:31.574
There are secrets here.
and I can trust no stranger.

151
00:16:32.616 --> 00:16:34.493
Ah. there you are.

152
00:16:36.328 --> 00:16:38.038
You're just in time for supper.

153
00:16:44.461 --> 00:16:48.756
The maesters tell me the fat of livestock
is beneficial to the bones.

154
00:16:48.757 --> 00:16:51.676
But I do wonder how something
so slippery in substance

155
00:16:51.677 --> 00:16:53.512
can truly be benign.

156
00:16:55.681 --> 00:16:57.182
Do try the wine. Lord Corlys.

157
00:16:58.267 --> 00:17:01.312
I find it wards off
the fetid air of this place.

158
00:17:06.817 --> 00:17:09.277
What are you about. Hightower?

159
00:17:09.278 --> 00:17:11.864
Is this some kind of final repast?

160
00:17:12.823 --> 00:17:15.366
Pigeon pie before the executioner's block?

161
00:17:15.367 --> 00:17:16.744
On the contrary.

162
00:17:17.786 --> 00:17:20.581
We hope to enjoy the pleasure
of your company for quite some time.

163
00:17:21.248 --> 00:17:24.293
You will be of great assistance to us
in our little endeavor.

164
00:17:25.502 --> 00:17:28.714
- As what? A hostage?
- Hm.

165
00:17:29.965 --> 00:17:32.091
Does the savage queen
harbor such a tender heart

166
00:17:32.092 --> 00:17:35.720
that she should cast away her crown
for the sake of her wayward Hand?

167
00:17:35.721 --> 00:17:37.097
I think not.

168
00:17:38.641 --> 00:17:40.767
The Velaryons. however.

169
00:17:40.768 --> 00:17:43.645
with their lord as forfeit.
the men of Driftmark

170
00:17:43.646 --> 00:17:46.731
will think better
of entering King's Landing.

171
00:17:46.732 --> 00:17:50.361
And without them. the city will again
eat of its own disorder.

172
00:17:54.198 --> 00:17:56.240
How will that help

173
00:17:56.241 --> 00:17:58.369
when the Winter Wolves
are clawing at our gates?

174
00:18:05.751 --> 00:18:07.210
Do you know?

175
00:18:07.211 --> 00:18:10.380
More and more I am inclined

176
00:18:10.381 --> 00:18:11.840
to limit my diet...

177
00:18:13.384 --> 00:18:14.802
to the vegetable kingdom.

178
00:18:16.178 --> 00:18:18.055
Just as the people of Naathi do.

179
00:18:18.847 --> 00:18:21.182
If you have finished
with your instruction--

180
00:18:21.183 --> 00:18:22.935
What do you see in them. anyway?

181
00:18:23.936 --> 00:18:25.479
The Targaryen...

182
00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:28.106
element.

183
00:18:28.107 --> 00:18:32.194
You are a traveled man.
you have seen the world's wonders.

184
00:18:33.362 --> 00:18:37.908
Why limit yourself in tedious alliance
to the brutish and the incurious?

185
00:18:41.537 --> 00:18:44.122
Your wife. of course. was of their blood.

186
00:18:44.123 --> 00:18:46.375
That ended all too predictably.

187
00:18:49.211 --> 00:18:51.838
I would think. after having seen

188
00:18:51.839 --> 00:18:53.882
how they devour one of their own...

189
00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:58.721
I would like to return to my cell.

190
00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:01.390
As you please.

191
00:19:05.644 --> 00:19:06.978
Oh. Lord Corlys?

192
00:19:06.979 --> 00:19:08.230
Before you go...

193
00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.859
He was in uncommon good spirits...

194
00:19:12.985 --> 00:19:15.319
as though he were on the eve
of some great victory.

195
00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.697
He seems to believe that
with Lord Corlys as hos--

196
00:19:17.698 --> 00:19:19.450
Is this his "piece on the board"?

197
00:19:21.201 --> 00:19:23.286
What does the order or disorder
of King's Landing

198
00:19:23.287 --> 00:19:25.414
matter to us now
with an army at the gates?

199
00:19:26.165 --> 00:19:27.458
I'm supposed to be the king.

200
00:19:29.668 --> 00:19:31.627
What sort of ruler am I?

201
00:19:31.628 --> 00:19:36.049
Am I to sit by impotent while a madman
offers us up for the slaughter?

202
00:19:37.968 --> 00:19:39.887
And all of our men with us?

203
00:19:41.597 --> 00:19:43.223
Seems there's no escaping it.

204
00:19:44.349 --> 00:19:47.644
The dream some have of covering themselves
in everlasting glory...

205
00:19:49.146 --> 00:19:51.482
of somehow transcending
humanity's common fate.

206
00:19:54.943 --> 00:19:58.739
I am sorry about your friend.

207
00:20:02.034 --> 00:20:04.161
He gave himself to the dust.

208
00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:12.002
I could order the army to surrender.

209
00:20:12.586 --> 00:20:14.170
And then what?

210
00:20:14.171 --> 00:20:16.048
Have us all marched to the gallows?

211
00:20:18.759 --> 00:20:21.678
You could fly away on Tessarion.

212
00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:24.305
Without you as a pretext for--

213
00:20:24.306 --> 00:20:26.266
He would continue as he began.

214
00:20:28.018 --> 00:20:30.061
Where would I go?

215
00:20:30.062 --> 00:20:33.148
Who would receive a king
who left his own men to their ruin?

216
00:20:36.485 --> 00:20:38.821
I have no fear of insignificance. Gwayne.

217
00:20:42.825 --> 00:20:45.035
Rhaenyra may keep her crown.
for all I care.

218
00:20:48.705 --> 00:20:50.748
Frankly. it is outrageous.

219
00:20:50.749 --> 00:20:54.001
There is a campaign against me!
Jeering in the streets.

220
00:20:54.002 --> 00:20:57.296
My own daughter found
the doorstep of my city dwelling

221
00:20:57.297 --> 00:21:00.217
smeared with some sort of foul matter.

222
00:21:01.927 --> 00:21:04.095
I don't know what you
want me to do about it.

223
00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:05.347
My queen.

224
00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:07.266
With respect.

225
00:21:08.684 --> 00:21:11.853
In front of petitioners.
you named me responsible

226
00:21:11.854 --> 00:21:15.231
for the current financial
grievances in the city.

227
00:21:15.232 --> 00:21:16.566
I hardly be--

228
00:21:16.567 --> 00:21:17.860
Well. what have you done
to alleviate them?

229
00:21:18.986 --> 00:21:20.612
What can I do?

230
00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:24.533
I have advocated for a tax.
It has fallen on deaf ears.

231
00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:29.579
Our dribbles of gold are spent
as fast as they are gathered.

232
00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:33.876
It's as if I have been installed here
as some sort of scapegoat.

233
00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:40.173
Has there been any word from Lord Corlys?

234
00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:43.260
From Harrenhal?

235
00:21:46.513 --> 00:21:49.724
- And Daemon?
- Absent.

236
00:21:49.725 --> 00:21:52.310
The prince is on some...

237
00:21:52.311 --> 00:21:54.020
errand of his own.

238
00:21:54.021 --> 00:21:57.648
The Keepers say he flew out
of the city before dawn.

239
00:21:57.649 --> 00:22:01.360
The river host are but a day's march
from Tumbleton. Your Grace.

240
00:22:01.361 --> 00:22:03.946
and the Velaryon forces will be
at King's Landing on the morrow.

241
00:22:03.947 --> 00:22:07.283
I have a reputation to uphold.

242
00:22:07.284 --> 00:22:12.830
If Ser Adrian has been successful
in his endeavor. of course.

243
00:22:12.831 --> 00:22:15.499
then there is the small matter
of Harrenhal--

244
00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:17.836
Just take it.

245
00:22:18.754 --> 00:22:20.379
Your Grace?

246
00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:22.506
Return to the Twins

247
00:22:22.507 --> 00:22:25.844
and lead the men you have
left there to Harrenhal.

248
00:22:27.763 --> 00:22:30.014
This I will do gladly!

249
00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:32.016
If Aemond is dead. all the better.

250
00:22:32.017 --> 00:22:33.809
But in any case.
you shall occupy it again.

251
00:22:33.810 --> 00:22:35.311
and leave no place for him to return.

252
00:22:35.312 --> 00:22:36.563
My queen.

253
00:22:39.024 --> 00:22:41.025
We have seen something strange.

254
00:22:41.026 --> 00:22:42.652
- Vhagar?
- No.

255
00:22:42.653 --> 00:22:44.737
Sheepstealer. In the Riverlands.

256
00:22:44.738 --> 00:22:46.657
on the banks of the Blue Fork
near Fairmarket.

257
00:22:47.658 --> 00:22:49.325
That is unexpected. He's not known--

258
00:22:49.326 --> 00:22:51.036
Your Grace. he has a rider.

259
00:22:52.412 --> 00:22:55.164
- A new rider?
- I could not say.

260
00:22:55.165 --> 00:22:57.376
We gave chase. but lost him in the hills.

261
00:23:02.631 --> 00:23:04.674
That head Daemon brought to you.

262
00:23:04.675 --> 00:23:06.842
can you say in honesty
you've had no doubts?

263
00:23:06.843 --> 00:23:09.845
He was long in the Riverlands.
and now Sheepstealer

264
00:23:09.846 --> 00:23:12.848
is sighted there with a rider
he assured you was dead.

265
00:23:12.849 --> 00:23:14.809
And in that same moment.

266
00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:17.478
he has absented himself
without explanation.

267
00:23:17.479 --> 00:23:19.897
I have known him to lie.
but this is a great--

268
00:23:19.898 --> 00:23:22.858
You and I have known him to be
capable of far worse than lies.

269
00:23:22.859 --> 00:23:27.154
He has chafed since you arrived here
over your restraint in wielding power.

270
00:23:27.155 --> 00:23:29.407
He is impetuous and impatient.

271
00:23:29.408 --> 00:23:31.826
Who can say what alliance
he may have formed in secret

272
00:23:31.827 --> 00:23:34.997
- when he found you lacking.
- He has sworn to serve me.

273
00:23:36.331 --> 00:23:38.708
I cannot believe that now.
when I need him most.

274
00:23:38.709 --> 00:23:40.168
- that he would--
- Forgive me.

275
00:23:45.298 --> 00:23:46.425
Your Grace.

276
00:23:50.095 --> 00:23:54.391
But is there anything Daemon could do
that you would truly not believe?

277
00:23:59.312 --> 00:24:00.856
Fetch Ser Addam.

278
00:24:09.364 --> 00:24:11.574
They say it is the strength
of the sun in Volantis

279
00:24:11.575 --> 00:24:13.452
that makes for such sweetness
in the grape.

280
00:24:14.953 --> 00:24:17.246
If you mean to console me for this folly

281
00:24:17.247 --> 00:24:19.749
with Volantene wines.
you're much mistaken.

282
00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:22.418
Your Grace. I beg you. reconsider.

283
00:24:22.419 --> 00:24:25.421
At Maidenpool. we might take ship
for Casterly Rock instead.

284
00:24:25.422 --> 00:24:27.882
No. I am decided on Braavos.

285
00:24:27.883 --> 00:24:29.967
How much further must we ride?

286
00:24:29.968 --> 00:24:31.386
Some days still to the port.

287
00:24:32.471 --> 00:24:34.597
Braavos will prove itself
a most cultivated city.

288
00:24:34.598 --> 00:24:35.932
I assure you.

289
00:24:36.558 --> 00:24:38.060
Perhaps even a home from home.

290
00:24:42.939 --> 00:24:43.774
Whoa.

291
00:24:44.608 --> 00:24:47.401
My good woman. what is it you flee?

292
00:24:47.402 --> 00:24:49.070
An army marches this way.

293
00:24:49.071 --> 00:24:51.363
- Some thousand strong.
- Which army?

294
00:24:51.364 --> 00:24:53.949
My daughter said she saw
the red fish on the white.

295
00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:56.535
- The Mootons.
- That's where we are going. to Maidenpool.

296
00:24:56.536 --> 00:24:59.205
We must keep moving.
Turn back if you can.

297
00:24:59.206 --> 00:25:00.707
Mootons are sworn to Rhaenyra.

298
00:25:02.167 --> 00:25:03.794
They can't have heard about me?

299
00:25:17.015 --> 00:25:18.517
The road is lost to us.

300
00:25:19.518 --> 00:25:22.061
We must fall back to Rook's Rest.

301
00:25:22.062 --> 00:25:24.522
We can't go back there.
We may have been discovered.

302
00:25:24.523 --> 00:25:27.400
There is an army coming for us
and we have no place to shelter.

303
00:25:28.819 --> 00:25:31.779
There are thick walls at Rook's Rest
and enough men to defend them.

304
00:25:31.780 --> 00:25:34.866
It shall be refuge for His Grace
till Mooton's host has passed.

305
00:25:40.580 --> 00:25:41.748
You must be famished.

306
00:25:43.166 --> 00:25:45.127
It's a long journey from King's Landing.

307
00:25:47.546 --> 00:25:48.547
Yes.

308
00:25:50.590 --> 00:25:51.883
And fraught. no doubt.

309
00:25:53.426 --> 00:25:55.428
If half the tales I have heard
about the King's Road are true.

310
00:25:59.099 --> 00:26:01.392
How is it that the two of you

311
00:26:01.393 --> 00:26:02.894
came to know one another?

312
00:26:07.023 --> 00:26:08.441
She saved my life.

313
00:26:10.569 --> 00:26:12.236
At whose behest?

314
00:26:12.237 --> 00:26:13.446
Your lord's?

315
00:26:14.072 --> 00:26:15.907
I generally follow my own dictates.

316
00:26:18.577 --> 00:26:21.246
Aemond. I still don't understand
who this woman is.

317
00:26:23.206 --> 00:26:24.332
Mm.

318
00:26:25.625 --> 00:26:27.627
She is a lady.

319
00:26:29.171 --> 00:26:30.964
And a maester. of sorts.

320
00:26:33.175 --> 00:26:36.011
The care of the castle
has fallen to her for now.

321
00:26:38.430 --> 00:26:43.435
I've decided to stay here with her
and make this place my seat.

322
00:26:46.062 --> 00:26:47.855
Your seat?

323
00:26:47.856 --> 00:26:49.858
Was that not what you yourself suggested?

324
00:26:51.109 --> 00:26:52.902
A new fortress from which to rule.

325
00:26:52.903 --> 00:26:56.780
Rhaenyra has the throne
and six dragons to her name.

326
00:26:56.781 --> 00:26:59.950
It is she who rules now. as much as we
might wish it otherwise.

327
00:26:59.951 --> 00:27:01.202
Mm.

328
00:27:01.203 --> 00:27:04.915
Rhaenyra's dragons
are ridden by commoners.

329
00:27:06.583 --> 00:27:10.502
She's defiled our great house.
diminished the Iron Throne.

330
00:27:10.503 --> 00:27:12.505
and sowed the seeds of her own ruin.

331
00:27:14.132 --> 00:27:15.634
She will certainly fail.

332
00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:20.889
And we will raise our own throne.

333
00:27:22.599 --> 00:27:25.560
In the mud of the Riverlands.

334
00:27:27.771 --> 00:27:29.272
A new dawn is coming.

335
00:27:32.150 --> 00:27:34.402
A new line of unsullied kings.

336
00:27:37.739 --> 00:27:39.449
We need only to bide our time.

337
00:27:41.826 --> 00:27:43.328
And you. Mother.

338
00:27:45.247 --> 00:27:47.040
You will wait with us.

339
00:27:48.500 --> 00:27:50.751
You have worth yet to offer.

340
00:27:50.752 --> 00:27:53.505
I'm sure your mother will wish to move on.

341
00:27:54.965 --> 00:27:57.424
Back to Oldtown. perhaps.

342
00:27:57.425 --> 00:27:59.551
Our climate doesn't seem to suit her.

343
00:27:59.552 --> 00:28:01.220
Mm. there's nothing for her there.

344
00:28:01.221 --> 00:28:02.304
I am all she has left.

345
00:28:02.305 --> 00:28:03.682
- There is Helaena.
- No!

346
00:28:04.599 --> 00:28:06.101
You'll stay with us.

347
00:28:10.981 --> 00:28:12.399
We're out of wood.

348
00:28:20.282 --> 00:28:23.701
I will not be coddled or admonished
like a witless child.

349
00:28:23.702 --> 00:28:25.912
Tread carefully with her. Aemond.

350
00:28:26.997 --> 00:28:28.872
She's come to do you some ill.

351
00:28:28.873 --> 00:28:30.583
She is my blood.

352
00:28:31.751 --> 00:28:33.210
And thus without blemish?

353
00:28:33.211 --> 00:28:36.172
She's always had her secrets.
most of them poorly kept.

354
00:28:37.257 --> 00:28:40.302
My designs for our future
did not include your mother.

355
00:28:41.011 --> 00:28:42.429
And there is the truth of it.

356
00:28:43.388 --> 00:28:44.848
You want me for yourself.

357
00:28:47.017 --> 00:28:48.977
There is a fog that surrounds her.

358
00:28:51.521 --> 00:28:53.982
She has come to do you some evil.

359
00:28:55.608 --> 00:28:58.236
You would be wise to keep
your dark thoughts to yourself.

360
00:29:06.328 --> 00:29:09.331
You Targaryen boys all want
the same thing. don't you?

361
00:30:01.299 --> 00:30:02.550
Tom Tangletongue. what news?

362
00:30:03.551 --> 00:30:07.262
Lord Mooton of Maidenpool.
he's dispatched an army.

363
00:30:07.263 --> 00:30:08.515
They're marching in haste.

364
00:30:09.933 --> 00:30:13.144
Have you not seen our Janos?
I thought he'd be with you.

365
00:30:14.187 --> 00:30:15.813
No. Where are they marching?

366
00:30:15.814 --> 00:30:17.981
They were commanded here. to Rook's Rest.

367
00:30:17.982 --> 00:30:20.859
But they're going
village to village. it seems.

368
00:30:20.860 --> 00:30:22.946
in search of your friend Lannister.

369
00:30:24.072 --> 00:30:26.157
Something about the queen's gold.

370
00:30:26.991 --> 00:30:29.786
They'll be here before we know it.
You'd best be on the move.

371
00:30:41.923 --> 00:30:44.634
I think you'll agree. Ser Tyland.
that you should give yourself up.

372
00:30:45.552 --> 00:30:46.886
She will flay me alive.

373
00:30:47.554 --> 00:30:49.555
No doubt. But once Mooton
has you in hand.

374
00:30:49.556 --> 00:30:51.515
he'll turn towards King's Landing.
and His Grace and I

375
00:30:51.516 --> 00:30:52.766
may yet slip away.

376
00:30:52.767 --> 00:30:54.143
Give the king to me and my men.

377
00:30:54.144 --> 00:30:56.145
We will ride hard
and escape Mooton's clutches.

378
00:30:56.146 --> 00:30:58.147
Oh. must you be so thick?

379
00:30:58.148 --> 00:30:59.815
Rhaenyra is hunting you.

380
00:30:59.816 --> 00:31:01.942
His Grace is not safe in your company.

381
00:31:01.943 --> 00:31:04.194
Turn yourself in
and give him the chance to flee.

382
00:31:04.195 --> 00:31:05.446
Him or you?

383
00:31:05.447 --> 00:31:07.448
It is the honorable thing to do.

384
00:31:07.449 --> 00:31:09.325
- Your Grace. for now. at least--
- No.

385
00:31:12.078 --> 00:31:13.495
No.

386
00:31:13.496 --> 00:31:15.123
Go where you will.

387
00:31:16.082 --> 00:31:17.292
Both of you.

388
00:31:18.334 --> 00:31:19.961
Preserve your own skins.

389
00:31:21.254 --> 00:31:22.838
But I shall run no more.

390
00:31:22.839 --> 00:31:24.923
If you do not run.
Your Grace. you will die.

391
00:31:24.924 --> 00:31:26.258
Then I'll die.

392
00:31:26.259 --> 00:31:27.886
But not as a fugitive.

393
00:31:30.263 --> 00:31:32.390
Unknown. Covered in dust.

394
00:31:33.099 --> 00:31:37.770
Not with an arrow in my back
or trapped like a fox in a hole.

395
00:31:39.022 --> 00:31:41.106
This is absurd.
Ser Tyland. I entreat you

396
00:31:41.107 --> 00:31:42.191
to reason with His Grace.

397
00:31:42.192 --> 00:31:43.318
I'll make my stand here.

398
00:31:45.570 --> 00:31:46.863
And be buried as a king.

399
00:31:48.531 --> 00:31:49.949
With my dragon.

400
00:31:53.745 --> 00:31:56.288
I will not have the histories
say that I was slain

401
00:31:56.289 --> 00:31:58.541
in ignominy by my own brother.

402
00:32:04.964 --> 00:32:07.050
If the king wishes to remain. then...

403
00:32:09.260 --> 00:32:11.094
I shall remain with him.

404
00:32:11.095 --> 00:32:13.223
I cannot leave him to face
an army meant for me.

405
00:32:21.564 --> 00:32:23.233
You're resolved in this then?

406
00:32:30.657 --> 00:32:31.991
Well then. my lords...

407
00:32:33.451 --> 00:32:35.995
it seems there is only one thing
left for me to do.

408
00:32:37.580 --> 00:32:39.540
May the Seven be ever at your side.

409
00:32:39.541 --> 00:32:41.542
You would abandon your master?

410
00:32:41.543 --> 00:32:43.878
I am a cripple. Ser Tyland.

411
00:32:46.005 --> 00:32:48.173
Humble enough to admit
that my presence in a fight

412
00:32:48.174 --> 00:32:49.717
would make no earthly difference.

413
00:32:52.762 --> 00:32:55.181
Of course. if my king
commanded me to stay...

414
00:32:57.183 --> 00:32:58.893
What Lord Larys says is true.

415
00:33:00.937 --> 00:33:02.814
He would be no use to us here.

416
00:33:03.982 --> 00:33:05.191
Well. then.

417
00:33:06.943 --> 00:33:10.113
It will be my duty to see
that King Aegon is remembered.

418
00:33:12.073 --> 00:33:15.450
His heroic last hours
immortalized through story...

419
00:33:15.451 --> 00:33:17.078
and song.

420
00:33:21.165 --> 00:33:22.542
Your Grace.

421
00:33:36.556 --> 00:33:37.765
Your Grace.

422
00:33:38.975 --> 00:33:40.268
Come. come. come.

423
00:34:30.943 --> 00:34:32.861
- Stay back!
- You swore to me.

424
00:34:32.862 --> 00:34:34.988
- You should not have come.
- Did you think she would not hear of this?

425
00:34:34.989 --> 00:34:37.784
Stay back! He does not heed me!

426
00:34:42.497 --> 00:34:43.498
<i>Daor!</i>

427
00:34:48.795 --> 00:34:50.046
<i>Daor!</i>

428
00:34:56.928 --> 00:34:59.179
What do you hope to do here?
In the reeds and the mud?

429
00:34:59.180 --> 00:35:00.889
Vhagar was here.

430
00:35:00.890 --> 00:35:02.349
Or near here. last I heard.

431
00:35:02.350 --> 00:35:03.892
We heard the same. but she is gone.

432
00:35:03.893 --> 00:35:05.394
Then I will fly in search of her.

433
00:35:05.395 --> 00:35:06.729
And if you find her?

434
00:35:07.480 --> 00:35:09.731
I thought I could do this. but I can't.

435
00:35:09.732 --> 00:35:12.694
I cannot live the way I have.
cut off from all who loved me.

436
00:35:13.486 --> 00:35:15.863
And so. you think by going
after Vhagar. you will...

437
00:35:17.115 --> 00:35:18.241
what?

438
00:35:18.825 --> 00:35:20.033
If I kill her.

439
00:35:20.034 --> 00:35:21.993
I will have paid
some of my debt to Rhaenyra.

440
00:35:21.994 --> 00:35:24.204
I would at least have grounds
to sue for her mercy.

441
00:35:24.205 --> 00:35:26.331
- You will more likely die.
- Then I will have paid all of it.

442
00:35:26.332 --> 00:35:28.710
I will die absolved
if I cannot live that way.

443
00:35:38.678 --> 00:35:39.846
Let me help you. then.

444
00:35:41.472 --> 00:35:43.099
You cannot battle Vhagar alone.

445
00:35:44.392 --> 00:35:46.144
But the two of us may yet prevail.

446
00:35:47.937 --> 00:35:49.480
Why would you do such a thing?

447
00:35:51.190 --> 00:35:53.860
I had no dragon either when I was young.
Did you know that?

448
00:35:55.236 --> 00:35:57.946
My mother died in childbed
when I was three years of age.

449
00:35:57.947 --> 00:35:59.823
My brother sank into sadness.

450
00:35:59.824 --> 00:36:02.201
I was alone. just as you have been.

451
00:36:05.997 --> 00:36:07.707
I should have done better. Rhaena.

452
00:36:16.090 --> 00:36:19.050
- You lie.
- I did not summon them.

453
00:36:19.051 --> 00:36:22.387
- You'd betray your own daughter?
- I have not. I swear it.

454
00:36:22.388 --> 00:36:23.639
She does not yet know who you are.

455
00:36:25.641 --> 00:36:26.808
Leave him.

456
00:36:26.809 --> 00:36:28.478
They will tear you from the sky.

457
00:36:31.230 --> 00:36:32.857
Run! Run!

458
00:36:47.497 --> 00:36:48.664
Go!

459
00:37:03.888 --> 00:37:05.180
- Call off your dragon!
- What is your agreement

460
00:37:05.181 --> 00:37:06.641
with Sheepstealer's rider?

461
00:37:07.225 --> 00:37:08.308
Answer carefully.

462
00:37:08.309 --> 00:37:10.310
You will not have
another chance to deceive me.

463
00:37:10.311 --> 00:37:11.812
I never wished to deceive you.

464
00:37:11.813 --> 00:37:13.606
- Then. speak!
- Call off your dragon.

465
00:37:21.948 --> 00:37:24.199
Please. Rhaenyra.

466
00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:25.618
She's not herself.

467
00:37:39.841 --> 00:37:40.883
Rhaena?

468
00:37:46.055 --> 00:37:47.431
It wasn't you.

469
00:37:57.775 --> 00:38:00.443
She was Sheepstealer's rider?

470
00:38:00.444 --> 00:38:02.488
All this time. you knew.

471
00:38:07.159 --> 00:38:08.536
This is finished!

472
00:38:21.048 --> 00:38:22.049
Move!

473
00:39:12.475 --> 00:39:15.686
- Your Grace!
- Help Daemon! Go!

474
00:39:16.896 --> 00:39:17.897
Go!

475
00:39:32.745 --> 00:39:33.913
With me!

476
00:39:41.837 --> 00:39:42.838
No!

477
00:39:51.514 --> 00:39:54.392
Escort the queen. I will finish this.

478
00:40:54.368 --> 00:40:57.162
It is magnificent in its way.

479
00:40:57.163 --> 00:41:00.499
I saw it once before
when I petitioned the queen.

480
00:41:04.837 --> 00:41:07.089
Do you know what it brings to my mind?

481
00:41:08.215 --> 00:41:11.761
A hundred sharp little cocks
all vying for attention.

482
00:41:13.387 --> 00:41:17.850
The queen wishes at the moment
to hear no more petitions.

483
00:41:18.809 --> 00:41:20.352
That is a mistake.

484
00:41:21.270 --> 00:41:22.854
I agree.

485
00:41:22.855 --> 00:41:25.024
There is villainy and violence
on her streets now.

486
00:41:27.026 --> 00:41:29.027
The people are afraid to go out by night.

487
00:41:29.028 --> 00:41:30.738
It is to her detriment only.

488
00:41:31.781 --> 00:41:35.951
Those who look to her for relief
now feel she's turned her back on them.

489
00:41:38.829 --> 00:41:42.707
I wished to hear from you
how you fare in this city.

490
00:41:42.708 --> 00:41:45.502
And if there are others
who may find it a consolation

491
00:41:45.503 --> 00:41:49.381
to come to me with their troubles
and have them considered.

492
00:41:50.716 --> 00:41:53.676
You make yourself her proxy.

493
00:41:53.677 --> 00:41:55.678
Someone must. Do you not agree?

494
00:41:55.679 --> 00:41:57.847
If she herself is reluctant.

495
00:41:57.848 --> 00:42:01.017
I can perhaps then bring
certain dilemmas before her

496
00:42:01.018 --> 00:42:04.605
when I judge her mood
to be more accommodating.

497
00:42:07.399 --> 00:42:09.360
You are changed.

498
00:42:12.196 --> 00:42:13.447
This...

499
00:42:14.031 --> 00:42:15.324
has changed you.

500
00:42:16.325 --> 00:42:20.120
My heart is with the downtrodden
as it has ever been.

501
00:42:20.121 --> 00:42:21.205
Is it?

502
00:42:21.831 --> 00:42:25.626
Or have you styled yourself a champion
in order to access these halls?

503
00:42:28.003 --> 00:42:29.088
Look at you.

504
00:42:30.089 --> 00:42:31.548
Standing at the foot of the throne

505
00:42:31.549 --> 00:42:33.883
wearing a silk worth a year
of my earnings.

506
00:42:33.884 --> 00:42:36.220
promising to whisper
into the ear of a queen.

507
00:42:37.555 --> 00:42:40.598
You thrill now to a tune
you once abhorred.

508
00:42:40.599 --> 00:42:43.351
Does it not occur to you
that from this position

509
00:42:43.352 --> 00:42:45.854
I may help those who have no avenue?

510
00:42:45.855 --> 00:42:49.024
What power do you have in truth?

511
00:42:50.526 --> 00:42:52.611
Except to flatter and cajole?

512
00:42:55.865 --> 00:42:56.866
Ah.

513
00:42:57.867 --> 00:42:59.285
Is that why you called me here?

514
00:43:00.494 --> 00:43:03.414
To look on the trappings so that
someone would hold you in awe?

515
00:43:06.125 --> 00:43:07.710
This was a mistake.

516
00:43:09.170 --> 00:43:11.462
How common I must seem to you.

517
00:43:11.463 --> 00:43:12.756
That will be all.

518
00:43:15.843 --> 00:43:17.928
Some advice. my lady.

519
00:43:19.346 --> 00:43:21.973
These people are not your own.

520
00:43:21.974 --> 00:43:23.767
You would do well to remember that.

521
00:43:25.144 --> 00:43:27.228
Within the walls of the highborn.

522
00:43:27.229 --> 00:43:31.275
a whore will always
and ever remain a whore.

523
00:43:53.839 --> 00:43:54.924
Find her a room.

524
00:43:55.716 --> 00:43:57.134
I do not wish to see her.

525
00:44:03.682 --> 00:44:05.017
Aemond?

526
00:44:08.312 --> 00:44:09.396
Mother.

527
00:44:21.116 --> 00:44:22.659
Your friend Alys.

528
00:44:22.660 --> 00:44:24.411
- She's not my friend.
- Oh.

529
00:44:25.788 --> 00:44:27.498
She doesn't want me to stay here.

530
00:44:28.123 --> 00:44:30.875
If I'm disturbing
some understanding between--

531
00:44:30.876 --> 00:44:32.210
No.

532
00:44:32.211 --> 00:44:34.295
- I should perhaps not have come.
- No.

533
00:44:34.296 --> 00:44:37.216
I will take my leave.
if that would behoove you.

534
00:44:38.467 --> 00:44:40.010
I'm glad you came.

535
00:44:44.014 --> 00:44:45.516
I brought you something.

536
00:44:51.355 --> 00:44:52.815
Spiced wine.

537
00:44:54.817 --> 00:44:57.736
I remember a time when you would
not fall asleep without it.

538
00:45:04.326 --> 00:45:05.953
Alys doesn't trust you.

539
00:45:14.920 --> 00:45:16.380
Who do you trust?

540
00:45:20.801 --> 00:45:21.802
I...

541
00:45:23.470 --> 00:45:25.347
I tried to kill Aegon.

542
00:45:35.441 --> 00:45:36.525
I know.

543
00:45:39.445 --> 00:45:40.863
My dear...

544
00:45:42.614 --> 00:45:44.033
foolish boy.

545
00:45:56.211 --> 00:45:57.129
Your Grace.

546
00:46:05.554 --> 00:46:06.764
No. stay.

547
00:46:22.488 --> 00:46:24.281
She implored me not to tell you.

548
00:46:31.246 --> 00:46:33.831
She could not face you.
I wished only to protect her.

549
00:46:33.832 --> 00:46:34.957
From what?

550
00:46:34.958 --> 00:46:36.502
What do you think I am?

551
00:46:38.087 --> 00:46:39.922
You are my wife.

552
00:46:40.506 --> 00:46:44.051
She's my daughter.
One I have long neglected.

553
00:46:47.221 --> 00:46:50.849
Was she not seeking. in all this.
my favor or yours?

554
00:46:53.060 --> 00:46:57.731
I have looked a hundred times
at that skull you brought...

555
00:46:59.441 --> 00:47:02.277
thinking it was the villain
who killed my son.

556
00:47:06.240 --> 00:47:07.990
I am sorry.

557
00:47:07.991 --> 00:47:10.953
but you must see now that
I kept no scheme against you.

558
00:47:13.288 --> 00:47:15.624
I did only what I thought was best.
Rhaenyra.

559
00:47:20.462 --> 00:47:21.630
Please.

560
00:47:25.551 --> 00:47:26.844
It's late.

561
00:48:03.005 --> 00:48:04.423
I am sorry.

562
00:48:06.675 --> 00:48:07.968
To Jace.

563
00:48:10.804 --> 00:48:11.721
To you.

564
00:48:11.722 --> 00:48:13.807
- You would have been queen.
- Enough.

565
00:48:33.744 --> 00:48:35.245
You will begin anew.

566
00:48:43.128 --> 00:48:46.298
More Hightower loyalists were found.
Alert the confessors.

567
00:48:50.969 --> 00:48:52.012
Ser Alyn.

568
00:48:53.388 --> 00:48:54.681
It was left for you.

569
00:49:28.215 --> 00:49:29.216
Alys.

570
00:49:33.762 --> 00:49:34.888
Idiot.

571
00:50:45.542 --> 00:50:47.377
<i>Dracarys!</i>

572
00:51:53.026 --> 00:51:55.946
<i>It was Rhaena he was hiding all along.</i>

573
00:51:58.865 --> 00:52:01.325
He lied. I did not lead you astray.

574
00:52:01.326 --> 00:52:04.078
And yet you cannot say he betrayed me

575
00:52:04.079 --> 00:52:06.497
so much as he would not
betray his daughter.

576
00:52:06.498 --> 00:52:07.915
This time.

577
00:52:07.916 --> 00:52:10.793
But does it not prove
he is willing to deceive you

578
00:52:10.794 --> 00:52:12.629
if he judges it necessary?

579
00:52:13.547 --> 00:52:15.589
And you've never done the same?

580
00:52:15.590 --> 00:52:17.675
I've acted only in your interests.

581
00:52:17.676 --> 00:52:19.845
You have sought to turn me from him.

582
00:52:20.929 --> 00:52:24.890
Pouring your honey in my ear.
whispering. encouraging.

583
00:52:24.891 --> 00:52:27.226
seeking to make me in your image.

584
00:52:27.227 --> 00:52:28.936
In my image?

585
00:52:28.937 --> 00:52:32.148
Your Grace. have I ever
counseled you to do aught

586
00:52:32.149 --> 00:52:35.401
but what Viserys
would have you do in his place?

587
00:52:35.402 --> 00:52:38.070
As you have ofttimes said.
is your own desire.

588
00:52:38.071 --> 00:52:41.408
Yes. and in hewing to his vision.
what have I reaped?

589
00:52:42.367 --> 00:52:44.535
Peace? Prosperity?

590
00:52:44.536 --> 00:52:46.872
Ah. the gratitude of my subjects.

591
00:52:54.963 --> 00:52:56.715
My father was not a dreamer.

592
00:52:58.216 --> 00:53:00.051
But his whole life was a dream.

593
00:53:03.638 --> 00:53:05.182
Do not lose faith.

594
00:53:07.017 --> 00:53:10.020
You are on the precipice
of a great victory.

595
00:53:12.063 --> 00:53:15.734
The uncertainties that oppress you
will soon be resolved.

596
00:53:16.735 --> 00:53:20.197
Those who oppose you will fall away.

597
00:53:21.656 --> 00:53:23.992
Even Aemond is all but vanquished.

598
00:53:24.993 --> 00:53:28.330
You will be queen
for many years after this.

599
00:53:29.331 --> 00:53:31.750
And your children's children after you.

600
00:53:36.922 --> 00:53:38.673
Just a little longer.

601
00:53:44.095 --> 00:53:45.305
Do you think...

602
00:53:46.723 --> 00:53:47.933
I am worthy?

603
00:53:50.602 --> 00:53:52.646
In this moment. my queen.

604
00:53:56.107 --> 00:53:57.609
Rhaenyra.

605
00:54:05.909 --> 00:54:08.245
I have never been more certain of it.

606
00:55:31.494 --> 00:55:34.164
A final stand then. Ser Tyland.

607
00:55:35.999 --> 00:55:37.375
Your Grace.

608
00:56:05.946 --> 00:56:10.492
We claim this land for Rhaenyra.
Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

609
00:56:11.743 --> 00:56:13.994
You will throw down your arms

610
00:56:13.995 --> 00:56:16.289
and make ready to swear your fealty.

611
00:56:21.419 --> 00:56:23.129
Oh. no. no. no. no. no.

612
00:56:23.838 --> 00:56:24.839
Your Grace?

613
00:56:26.841 --> 00:56:28.218
Will you flee after all?

614
00:56:45.902 --> 00:56:48.613
We shall not surrender to the false queen.

615
00:56:56.913 --> 00:56:58.748
Is that you. Tyland Lannister?

616
00:57:00.041 --> 00:57:01.960
Your queen's been looking for you.

617
00:57:03.753 --> 00:57:06.046
Tell us where the gold is.

618
00:57:06.047 --> 00:57:09.092
and you will die
with your ears still attached.

619
00:57:22.731 --> 00:57:24.399
Behold me now!

620
00:57:26.860 --> 00:57:28.695
I am Aegon Targaryen!

621
00:57:30.447 --> 00:57:33.032
Viserys' true heir!

622
00:57:33.033 --> 00:57:36.744
The sixth King of the Andals
and the Rhoynar

623
00:57:36.745 --> 00:57:38.328
and the First Men!

624
00:57:38.329 --> 00:57:41.248
I was anointed by the High Septon

625
00:57:41.249 --> 00:57:43.208
in the light of the Seven.

626
00:57:43.209 --> 00:57:47.422
And it is in their light
that I stand before you now!

627
00:57:49.299 --> 00:57:51.675
Strike me down!

628
00:57:51.676 --> 00:57:54.846
And the Stranger will take retribution.

629
00:57:56.389 --> 00:57:59.893
The Warrior's sword
will be judgment upon you.

630
00:58:03.730 --> 00:58:04.564
Yes.

631
00:58:05.190 --> 00:58:06.483
Yes. cowards.

632
00:58:07.567 --> 00:58:09.402
You might well retreat.

633
00:58:10.111 --> 00:58:12.405
For now you see me as I truly am!

634
00:58:13.907 --> 00:58:16.241
Dreadful in vengeance!

635
00:58:16.242 --> 00:58:19.454
Righteous and glorious!

636
00:58:30.548 --> 00:58:31.925
Sunfyre.

637
00:58:39.224 --> 00:58:40.517
Sunfyre.

638
00:58:42.185 --> 00:58:43.728
<i>Dracarys.</i>

639
00:58:45.730 --> 00:58:48.149
Run! Save yourselves!

640
00:59:28.231 --> 00:59:29.440
Oh.

641
00:59:31.985 --> 00:59:33.319
Decent ale. that.

642
00:59:35.822 --> 00:59:37.365
I thought you might enjoy it.

643
00:59:43.621 --> 00:59:44.831
I have had word...

644
00:59:45.999 --> 00:59:49.252
since we last spoke
of a most distressing incident.

645
00:59:50.044 --> 00:59:53.256
My whisperers tell me that
Daemon Targaryen struck you.

646
00:59:54.424 --> 00:59:55.842
In the street.

647
00:59:58.052 --> 01:00:01.055
In front of all the commoners passing by.

648
01:00:02.223 --> 01:00:06.311
An intolerable insult
to someone of your stature.

649
01:00:08.271 --> 01:00:09.771
But then...

650
01:00:09.772 --> 01:00:12.608
it's almost to be
expected from those people.

651
01:00:12.609 --> 01:00:14.360
She did tell me not to go into town.

652
01:00:15.278 --> 01:00:17.154
- To be fair.
- Ludicrous.

653
01:00:17.155 --> 01:00:19.324
A man needs his sustenance and cheer.

654
01:00:21.451 --> 01:00:25.788
But it is obvious Rhaenyra and her ilk
regard you only as a tool.

655
01:00:27.790 --> 01:00:30.210
To be used and reprimanded.

656
01:00:32.670 --> 01:00:34.464
Whereas I understand...

657
01:00:35.965 --> 01:00:37.383
who you really are.

658
01:00:42.805 --> 01:00:45.141
You said last time...

659
01:00:47.268 --> 01:00:49.145
that you could give me a lordship.

660
01:00:51.314 --> 01:00:52.649
And a castle.

661
01:00:54.692 --> 01:00:55.777
Honeyholt.

662
01:00:57.612 --> 01:00:58.780
Honeyholt?

663
01:01:00.865 --> 01:01:02.492
Honeyholt is a trifle.

664
01:01:04.244 --> 01:01:08.706
It seems that Driftmark itself
may soon be without a master.

665
01:01:10.541 --> 01:01:12.710
Lord of the Tides.

666
01:01:14.712 --> 01:01:16.381
What do you think of that?

667
01:01:24.722 --> 01:01:26.557
They will laugh at you no more...

668
01:01:27.642 --> 01:01:29.352
when they see you as you are.

669
01:01:33.648 --> 01:01:34.816
No.

670
01:01:36.859 --> 01:01:38.194
They will burn.
